From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pmos-laurel-sprout <dev@laurel.invalid>
Date: 2026-08-13
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: sm6125: add MPSS transport nodes (v2, disabled)

Downstream-only v2 patch for the frozen 6.1 fork at
77de535b8dbd8f483b5802c8937cb714bab5b485.

Adds the MPSS (modem) remoteproc PAS transport that the WCN3990 needs to
receive QMI WLFW over QRTR (glink-edge "mpss", channel IPCRTR), while the
WCN3990 first-probe node (0001) stays intact.

The fork's qcom_q6v5_pas.c does not provide qcom,sm6115/sm6125-mpss-pas;
qcom,sm8150-mpss-pas resolves to mpss_resource_init (pas_id 4, smem 421,
minidump 3, proxy cx+mss, firmware modem.mdt, ssctl 0x12) which matches the
vendor SM6125 MPSS. A single power-domain <&rpmpd SM6125_VDDCX> is used so
adsp_pds_attach() takes the single-domain path (dev->pm_domain), avoiding
the cx/mss name mismatch.

The remoteproc_mpss node is added with status = "disabled" to keep the v2
build-ready and preserve the current boot behavior (MPSS not started).
Board-level enablement (&remoteproc_mpss { status = "okay"; }) is deferred
to the authorized physical-test phase only. No MMC/SDIO, no iommus.

Signed-off-by: pmos-laurel-sprout <dev@laurel.invalid>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125.dtsi | 66 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 66 insertions(+)
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125.dtsi
index f43b005..b71b246 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6125.dtsi
@@ -361,6 +361,34 @@
 		hwlocks = <&tcsr_mutex 3>;
 	};
 
+	smp2p-mpss {
+		compatible = "qcom,smp2p";
+		qcom,smem = <435>, <428>;
+
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 70 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		mboxes = <&apcs_glb 14>;
+
+		qcom,local-pid = <0>;
+		qcom,remote-pid = <1>;
+
+		modem_smp2p_out: master-kernel {
+			qcom,entry-name = "master-kernel";
+			#qcom,smem-state-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
+		modem_smp2p_in: slave-kernel {
+			qcom,entry-name = "slave-kernel";
+			interrupt-controller;
+			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+		};
+
+		wlan_smp2p_in: wlan-wpss-to-ap {
+			qcom,entry-name = "wlan";
+			interrupt-controller;
+			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+		};
+	};
+
 	soc {
 		#address-cells = <1>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
@@ -715,6 +743,39 @@
 			interrupt-controller;
 			interrupts = <GIC_PPI 9 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 		};
+
+		remoteproc_mpss: remoteproc@6080000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,sm8150-mpss-pas";
+			reg = <0x06080000 0x100>;
+
+			interrupts-extended = <&intc GIC_SPI 307 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+					      <&modem_smp2p_in 0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+					      <&modem_smp2p_in 1 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+					      <&modem_smp2p_in 2 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+					      <&modem_smp2p_in 3 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+					      <&modem_smp2p_in 7 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+			interrupt-names = "wdog", "fatal", "ready",
+					  "handover", "stop-ack", "shutdown-ack";
+
+			clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_XO_CLK_SRC>;
+			clock-names = "xo";
+
+			power-domains = <&rpmpd SM6125_VDDCX>;
+
+			memory-region = <&modem_mem>;
+
+			qcom,smem-states = <&modem_smp2p_out 0>;
+			qcom,smem-state-names = "stop";
+
+			status = "disabled";
+
+			glink-edge {
+				interrupts = <GIC_SPI 68 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+				label = "mpss";
+				qcom,remote-pid = <1>;
+				mboxes = <&apcs_glb 12>;
+			};
+		};
 	};
 
 	timer {
